+### 1824 — libssh2 adapter preserves operation scope and nonblocking argument identity (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: Channel read/write timeout cancellation shut down the shared socket bridge; channel opens rejected `rekeying` before entering the session gate and started their deadline only after gate admission; each rekey caller owned the connection-global KEX; and concurrent writes could resume libssh2's single per-channel write state with a different payload after `EAGAIN`. Credential results were checked against factory capabilities but not the caller-provided allowlist.
+- REWORK: Socket-service cancellation now retires only its independently cancellable readiness operation. Channel opens may queue behind rekey under their original bounded deadline. One bounded shared rekey flight coalesces trigger reasons and lets a canceled caller detach while KEX continues. Per-channel FIFO gates retain exact write arguments across `EAGAIN`, with queued bytes still reserved against the caller cap. Returned credential algorithms must belong to both adapter capabilities and the request allowlist.
+- CONFORMANCE: Deterministic loopback regressions prove canceled and timed-out reads leave sibling channels and the session ready; an open times out while rekey is deliberately suspended and a second queued open succeeds afterward; two rekey triggers produce one KEX while the first caller cancels; four concurrent same-channel payloads survive forced bridge backpressure byte-exactly; and a supported-but-disallowed credential algorithm fails before authentication.
+- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 23 tests/3 suites; strict Swift format and `git diff --check` pass; `make validate-core` passes 357 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; `make validate-libssh2`, `make test-libssh2-source-gates`, and `make native-apple-matrix` all exit 0. The four M3 semantics remain explicit `unsupported` states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
+
+### 1758 — libssh2 adapter loopback conformance closes review round 2 (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: libssh2 keeps channel-open and reply-requiring global-request nonblocking state on the shared session, so actor reentrancy across `EAGAIN` allowed a second open to resume the first open's state. The custom send/receive callback ABI also requires negative socket errors directly; returning `-1` plus `errno=EAGAIN` made ordinary backpressure appear as a disconnect.
+- REWORK: A bounded FIFO session-operation gate now holds one permit across every channel-open, client-rekey, and keepalive/global-request `EAGAIN` sequence while independent channel payload I/O remains interleavable. Callback would-block paths return `-EAGAIN`. Timeout adaptation uses structured tasks and joins the losing branch; bridge shutdown marks terminal state, closes the injected connection, cancels and joins every queued service task, and only then discards buffers or frees engine state.
+- CONFORMANCE: A serialized macOS loopback fixture starts ephemeral OpenSSH with an in-memory P-256 external signer and proves host-policy-before-credential ordering, approved public-key authentication, direct-tcpip echo, concurrent exec opens, exec/stdin upload, server-rekey traffic survival, manual client rekey, keepalive transmission, five connected read/cancel races, and three successful connect/close resource baselines. The four M3 semantics remain explicit `unsupported` reports owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
+- VERIFICATION: Strict recursive `swift-format` and `git diff --check`, `make validate-core` (353 tests/31 suites), `make validate-libssh2`, `make test-libssh2-source-gates`, and `make native-apple-matrix` all exit 0. `task-board validate` exits 0 and reports only the known story aggregate mismatch while this child is in development; no status or unsupported semantic is bypassed.
+
+### 1454 — libssh2 adapter review rework closes async ownership gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: Actor isolation serialized synchronous libssh2 calls but not the socket service work awaited between `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN` retries. Reentrant progress calls could snapshot the same outbound prefix, issue duplicate writes, and later remove inconsistent byte counts; suspended operations also retained channel/session pointers while teardown could free them.
+- REWORK: Socket progress now has one queued owner with exact-once partial drains. Channel reads enforce one pending operation per stream, writes reserve against the per-channel queued-byte cap, all pending gauges are live, and cancel/reset/close marks disposition then waits for tracked pointer users before bounded free. Session/open/connect teardown paths similarly drain active owners and serialize concurrent teardown.
+- REWORK: Upload has an overall deadline and rejects oversized source chunks; timeout racing returns without waiting for a non-cooperative injected dependency. External signer work is explicitly tracked, notification-driven rather than 1 ms polled, cancelled, and joined. Connect failures retain their pre-teardown phase, timeout/cancellation counters reconcile, and automatic keepalive failures consume the configured miss budget before fatal teardown.
+- VERIFICATION: Focused adapter coverage grew from 7 to 11 tests, adding forced overlapping socket writes (exact bytes, maximum concurrency one), joined signer cancellation, resolution timeout phase/counter evidence, and 20 repeated connect-cancel resource baselines. Strict format/diff checks, `make validate-core` (349 tests/30 suites), `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe Apple matrix all exit 0.
+- BOARD: `task-board validate` exits 0 but retains the known `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for `STORY-260715-lkshfz`: this child is in development while the story remains `to-dev` because its unfinished hard blocker suppresses automatic aggregation. No dependency or parent status was bypassed.
+
+### 0351 — Pinned libssh2 adapter joins the macOS provider and harness graphs (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- IMPLEMENTATION: `ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter` is the sole Swift target importing the pinned static libssh2/OpenSSL XCFramework. A serialized transport actor drives custom send/receive callbacks in nonblocking mode over the injected `SSHTCPConnection`; bounded async bridges turn socket and external-Keychain-signer progress into `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN` without blocking a provider executor.
+- SECURITY: The adapter applies explicit KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC allowlists with no SHA-1/CBC fallback, delivers the exact raw host-key blob plus negotiated host-key method and canonical SHA-256 fingerprint to policy before credential lookup, and carries only opaque credential references/public signing material across Core. Engine prose and endpoint/user/command data never enter errors or typed diagnostics.
+- DECISION: Consumer-driven receive credit, RFC channel-open reasons, exact exec-exit presence/`coreDumped`, and deep server-KEX/keepalive reporting are all emitted as `unsupported`, owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`. Client rekey, server-rekey protocol handling, bounded channel I/O, exec/stdin upload, and forced `keepalive@openssh.com` transmission remain implemented M0 behavior; no unavailable value is inferred from libssh2 internals.
+- ANOMALY: Xcode's generated package scheme copied both library-style XCFramework module maps to one custom `Release/include/module.modulemap`, producing a deterministic multiple-producer error once the libssh2 and native-fixture graphs met. The Apple matrix now keeps Xcode's existing device/simulator/native checks and uses isolated dual-architecture SwiftPM builds with `-application-extension` for the macOS provider/harness; the stripped release harness check verifies libssh2's intentionally hidden local rekey symbol separately from exported HEV symbols.
+- VERIFICATION: Strict recursive Swift format lint, `make validate-core` (345 tests/30 suites), `make validate-libssh2`, pinned-source tamper gates, and the revised Apple matrix all exit 0. Focused adapter tests cover bounded partial transport I/O, oversized-read rejection, async signer EAGAIN, explicit deferred capability states, and 20 repeated failed handshakes returning sessions/channels/sockets/tasks/custom allocations/buffers to zero.
+
 ### 0246 — SSH M0 viability keeps operational invariants and makes four evidence gaps typed
 - DECISION: ADR-023 is now exhaustive in `.spec/ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md` and `SSHConformanceRequirement`: 16 operational/security requirements are `m0ViabilityMandatory`; consumer-driven receive credit/cap, RFC channel-open rejection reasons, exact exec-exit presence/`coreDumped`, and deep server-KEX/keepalive observability are `m3Deferred(ownerTaskID: "TASK-260728-3cveay")`.
 - IMPLEMENTATION: `SSHDeferredSemanticReport` exposes `reported`, `notReported`, and `unsupported`. Exact receive-credit policy/snapshots, open reasons, exit metadata, KEX generation, window/server-rekey/keepalive metrics, and manual keepalive RTT now require one of those states; no default zero/false or mandatory full-fidelity policy remains. Host-before-auth, approved public-key auth, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client and server rekey handling, bounded buffers/backpressure, cancellation/lifecycle, Keychain-only credential references, keepalive transmission, available metrics, and privacy-safe errors remain mandatory.
