.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:31:| Apple target integration | The static/source graph builds for the macOS harness and packet-tunnel extension with extension-safe public APIs. iOS delivery remains deferred by ADR-024, not by this SSH decision. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:32:| Candidate-neutral injection | Core imports no engine types. TCP readiness/I/O, host policy, credential provider, clock, cancellation, logger, observer, metrics, identity generation, and experiment recording remain injected and fakeable. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:33:| Host key before authentication | Exact raw wire key, negotiated host-key algorithm, and canonical SHA-256 fingerprint reach the host policy before credential lookup or any authentication request. Unknown, changed, algorithm-rejected, and policy-rejected hosts fail closed before auth. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:34:| Approved public-key authentication | Noninteractive Ed25519 plus an approved deployed fallback work through opaque external signing. Password prompts, agent forwarding, and silent algorithm downgrade are not fallbacks. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:37:| Exec and stdin upload | One accepted exec request exposes bounded stdin/stdout/stderr and long-lived framing. Relay upload uses exec/stdin only, drains output concurrently, and never invokes SFTP. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:38:| Client-initiated rekey | Byte-threshold, time-threshold, test, and manual triggers use the production KEX path under active traffic. Rekey failure/timeout stays connection-fatal. |
